            <description><![CDATA[
<h2>LazyTasks 2.1.3</h2>
<ul>
    <li><b>Per-project secrets</b> — projects can hold secret variables (API keys, admin credentials) so agents in fresh workspaces can run the app they're working on. Add keys via the <code>SECRETS</code> badge or import a <code>.env</code> from the clipboard. Values are write-only and never leave this machine; key names sync so a second Mac shows what still needs entering.</li>
    <li><b>Per-project Cloudflare accounts</b> — assign an account once per project and every session runs wrangler as that account. Profiles share the <code>~/.cf-profiles</code> convention; tokens never leave the machine.</li>
    <li><b>Issue editing + self-assign</b> — edit issues right from LazyTasks, and new issues assign to you by default. Description fields are now proper multi-line editors.</li>
    <li><b>A livelier home</b> — issues handled, PRs shipped, day streak, "The Garden" contribution heatmap of your sessions, and Field Notes with fun facts from your ledger.</li>
    <li><b>Shipping tidies up</b> — "Ship it" closes the session's terminal window, and self-merged issues vanish from Open Issues immediately.</li>
    <li><b>Instant issue actions</b> — create, edit, label, assign, and close apply on the spot, reconciled against GitHub behind the scenes.</li>
</ul>
            ]]></description>
